          "citation": "2024 WY 37, 545 P.3d 856",
          "court": "Wyoming Supreme Court",
          "year": 2024,
          "date_decided": "2024-04-01",
          "holding": "The Court affirmed termination, holding that whether the Department made reasonable efforts is assessed case by case, that its efforts must be accessible and tailored to the parent, and that a case plan adapted to a mother's intellectual disability satisfied the standard.",
          "relevance": "The Court addressed the parent's argument that the Americans with Disabilities Act required further accommodation of her intellectual disability in the case plan.",
          "quote": "We assess on a case-by-case basis whether sufficient evidence exists to demonstrate the Department made reasonable efforts to rehabilitate the family",
